<vertex eid="17"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered Yes" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">E01 [YES]
B3 has excess low-drive spikes?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">E01 | B3 has excess low-drive spikes?

Status: YES

Method: Hierarchical / input and cyclical

Scope / coordinates: B3 g0-b3; Allen 541563728; 200/250/310 pA; recorded bias; nseg x9; CVode 1e-10; 2100 ms.

Remaining search space: Low-drive exact-count agreement versus at least one excess-count row at 200/250 pA.

Binary predicate: At least one of the 200/250 pA model counts exceeds its matched human count.

Decision limit: Exact counts: human 1/5 at 200/250 pA; the 310 pA control is 10.

Recorded observation: B3 gives 4/8/10 versus human 1/5/10 at 200/250/310 pA.

YES: Localize the low-drive excess while retaining the 310 pA control.

NO: Low-drive excess is absent; inspect other response failures independently.

Next check: Use E02-E05 to retain tested exclusions; no additional evaluation is authorized.

Unresolved after either answer: Correct count at 310 pA is neither shared-input nor waveform validation.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-e-gain/stage-close-decision.json

