<vertex eid="20"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered Yes" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">E02 [YES]
Initiation is axon-first?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">E02 | Initiation is axon-first?

Status: YES

Method: Structural dissection / initiation

Scope / coordinates: B3 at active SP3 inputs, including sweeps 50/53/56; soma and axon threshold crossings.

Remaining search space: Axon-first versus simultaneous or soma-first initiation under the recorded detector.

Binary predicate: The recorded axon crossing precedes the soma crossing at the active inputs in scope.

Decision limit: Strict ordering of the recorded crossings; retain measured lead and numerical resolution from stage-g0, not a new threshold.

Recorded observation: Stage-g0 and closure report axon-first initiation; it persists in the tested passive interventions.

YES: Retain the initiation site and examine the tested passive levers.

NO: Localize initiation before interpreting passive changes as gain corrections.

Next check: Keep B3 axonal initiation fixed when formulating the next bounded gain test.

Unresolved after either answer: Axon-first initiation does not establish the right count, width, or H01 region map.

