Import alone reproduces the failure?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">P02 | Import alone reproduces the failure?

Status: YES

Method: Functional isolation / importer boundary

Scope / coordinates: Offline H01Archive.load of 104 largest components; same BrainCell SWC reader, no simulation.

Remaining search space: Failure reproduced without network initialization or stepping, or only later in the pipeline.

Binary predicate: The standalone import reproduces the branch-construction failure.

Decision limit: Same from_points exception on the released component; exact node/parent structure retained.

Recorded observation: Seven of 104 largest components fail. Near-coincident 0.032 um nodes interact with reader np.allclose at coordinates near 3000 um; both leaf and branch-point cases occur.

YES: Keep the fault localized to import/reader geometry handling.

NO: Investigate construction context and subsequent stages.

Next check: A future repair needs a reproducer for both leaf and branch-point cases, preserved geometry/provenance, and full 104-component audit before rerunning 40 cells.

Unresolved after either answer: This artifact applies no repair and does not authorize collapsing nodes or inventing cable.

