Status: NO

Method: Hierarchical / reference before transfer

Scope / coordinates: HL5MN1 source fit, 100/150 pA, sweeps 44/35, original and half dt.

Remaining search space: Exact counts agree at both inputs, or at least one differs.

Binary predicate: The source model reproduces both matched donor counts.

Decision limit: Exact counts; retain separate repeat bands. Latency limits use |dt-pair difference| x2.95.

Recorded observation: Human 14/34; model 16/30 at both dt values. Source reproduction rejected.

YES: Continue waveform and transfer qualification.

NO: Isolate unchanged source-condition mismatch before using this donor as qualified physiology.

Next check: Audit initial state, bias, temperature, waveform and mechanism conventions under a frozen source model; preserve two-input constraints.

Unresolved after either answer: Halving-dt count agreement rules out that count change over the tested pair, not every numerical issue.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-sst-reproduction.md
docs/evidence/h01-donors/stage-hl5mn1-decision.json

